<!DOCTYPE airframe SYSTEM "../airframe.dtd">
<airframe name="Disco">
  <description>
    Parrot Disco Fixedwing, airframe to validate all onboard functionally
    + FLIGHTCONTROLLER: Default Parrot C.H.U.C.K.
    + ACTUATORS:        Default Servos
    + ESSC:             Default ESC 
    + GNSS:             Default uBlox M8N
    + AIRSPEED:         Default MS4515DO
    + TELEMETRY:        Default WiFi, 868 or optionally 4G module
    + CURRENT:          Default Build in V/A sensing
    + RC RX:            OpenR-XSR set to SBus output

    NOTES:

    + All kinds of info https://fccid.io/2AG6I-DISCO
    + Uses PAPARAZZI "standard" radio channel settings TAER and Aerospace sign convention
    + One could make a flightplan mimicking exact default behavior of Parrot assisted flight
    + Tested with Firmware v1.7.1, considder updating to this Disco firmware version if not done already
    + Can use Enhanced Total Energy Control System (ETECS) for control
    + Flash the PPRZ firmware via WiFi, 4G or USB
    + Enlarged battery bay to fit a high capacity 5200 mAh 3S LiPo battery. The all-up weight (AUW)) of the airframe will be ~150g more
      Center of gravity still the same, flighttime doubles...
    + Regular Telemetry is possible via USB to FTDI serial to Modem, added kernel drivers see:
      https://wiki.paparazziuav.org/wiki/Howto.crosscompile_for_parrot_drones
      https://wiki.paparazziuav.org/wiki/Use_the_USB_port_on_Parrot_Drones
    + Bottom camera can used just for some mapping, not high resolution but still fun...
    + The Parrot C.H.U.C.K. can be removed from Disco and placed in a regular other RC aircraft
    + If you change your control from ETECS to Classic or New make sure to disable the settings/estimation/ac_char
    + AddedOption to fly with 12c 11000mAh LiIon battery, expect flighttimes of 100+ minutes at 15m/s
    + PPRZLink v2 advised for TCAS fun
    + OpenRX XSR but e.g a Spektrum DSMX Orange R620X Receiver with SBus out possible
    + If no units are specified, the values are in SI units (m, s, rad, m/s, m/s^2, etc.)

    WIP:
    + It flies well, still not all gains are tuned to optimum
    + The front cam is not yet fully supported with internal code, however successful video recording, streaming already possible with current mykonos module
    + Sonar needs to be put to good use e.g. last part of flare in landing
    + Investigate effectiveness scheduling for (high)speed adjustments on non transitional fixedwing

    Parrot Disco Photogrammeyty (with bottom camera recoring)
    
    Checklist:
    + tune your servo deflections per airframe (symmetric)
    + calibrate your magnetometer for the given battery
    + remove previous images before flight
    + trigger snapping images manually or in the flightplan
    + use Open Drone Map / ODMWeb (or similar)
    + make a movie with ffmpeg from the images via:

<!--
ls *.jpg | xargs -I {} echo "file '{}'" > images.txt
ffmpeg -f concat -safe 0 -i images.txt -c:v libx264 -crf 18 -profile:v baseline -level 3.0 -pix_fmt yuv420p -movflags faststart ./flight.mp4
-->

    Launching:
    1) Set TX to AUTO2
    2) Move nose to ground
    3) wait until props spins after a second or so,
    4) move aircraft slight pitch up
    5)Forcefully throw straight forward, not upwards, not downwards

 RC:
     If the RC receiver is e.g. an Orange R620X make sure to set modeswitch to Auto2 on your TX when binding!
     else if one would lose RC or switch of transmitter during Auto2 flight, it will hop to manual... very bad...

     A PPM receiver could theoretically be used, only for Linux ARCH no software to handle it is written (hint!)
     SUMD also. For the PPRZ Spektrum could also, but not if you also want to fly it with RC but without PPRZ as AP only original
     since Spektrum serial OUTPUT is not handled by the Parrot main AP
     So a Spektrum DSMX with SBUS out, as there are many on the market, works well.

     The setup of Transmitter is in such a way that one could fly without PPRZ just Parrot original AP with a 3rd party RC transmitter
     Thus modeswitch on 5 for well... mode

     Per Default

     TX Channel Nr  Function                        Control type        Comments
     |--------------|-------------------------------|------------------|-----------
     1              Roll                            Stick
     2              Pitch                           Stick
     3              Throttle                        Stick
     4              Yaw                             Stick               Used to set the Disco in loiter

     But we set our standard:

     1              Throttle                        Stick
     2              Roll                            Stick
     3              Pitch                           Stick
     4              Yaw                             Stick               Used to set the Disco in loiter

     setself        Gear                            3-position switch   Used to configure the piloting mode:
                      Auto-pilot with Parrot SkyController2 (Risky so better limit this one except if you teaching people to fly with Skycontroller student AND RCTX for teacher )
                      Auto-pilot with RC controller
                      Full manual with RC controller
     setself        Automatic Take-off/Landing      2-position switch   Used in “Auto-pilot with RC controller” mode
     setself        Start: SWx    Landing: SWy
     setself        Motor off in manual mode    SW?

     TIP:
     As soon as a RC receiver is connected to Disco, one has extra options in Freeflight Pro to set up the RC receiver channel order
     These values are then stored in the /data/lib/radio/map.sbus.cfg file on the Disco
     Telnet there, Mount the partition to RW and adjust at will if needed...

     As for the calibration in /data/lib/radio/calib.sbus.cfg

     These values are ONLY used when flying with RC on original Parrot Autopilot, NOT when flying with PPRZ as autopilot.
     But it is best to have them both set to the same values, so you can switch between PPRZ and Parrot AP without issues.
  </description>

